## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates understanding of multi-tenant GPU sharing in Kubernetes, MIG partition management, NVIDIA device plugin integration, and the ability to build custom resource controllers for quota enforcement with burst handling.

## Key Concepts

- GPU quota management in shared clusters
- MIG (Multi-Instance GPU) partitions
- CRD and controller patterns
- Resource enforcement via scheduler hints
- Observability for GPU workloads

## Code Example

```go
func (r *GPUQuotaReconciler) Reconcile(ctx context.Context, req ctrl.Request) (ctrl.Result, error) {
    ns := &corev1.Namespace{}
    if err := r.Get(ctx, req.NamespacedName, ns); err != nil {
        return ctrl.Result{}, client.IgnoreNotFound(err)
    }

    gpuQuota := &GPUQuota{}
    if err := r.Get(ctx, req.NamespacedName, gpuQuota); err != nil {
        return ctrl.Result{}, client.IgnoreNotFound(err)
    }

    available GPUs, err := r.getAvailableGPUs(ns.Name)
    if err != nil {
        return ctrl.Result{}, err
    }

    if gpuQuota.Spec.Burst.Enabled {
        if isWithinBurstWindow(gpuQuota) {
            return r.reconcileBurst(ctx, gpuQuota, availableGPUs)
        }
    }

    return r.enforceQuota(ctx, gpuQuota, availableGPUs)
}
```
